From 7f14cd32f576b0b0e6d69bcd9fce1263fcefcc2c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Abhishek <a.dandekar@tu.berlin>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 10:30:19 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(pcf): N5 policy authorization media components to PCC
 rules / QoS

Map the medComponents of an Npcf_PolicyAuthorization app session (TS 29.514,
e.g. from an MCPTT AF) to dynamic PCC rules and QoS decisions (TS 29.513
7.3) and notify the SMF (SmPolicyUpdateNotification):

- one PCC rule "mcx-<appSessionId>-<medCompN>" per media component, flow
  informations from all (enabled) media sub components fDescs; the
  direction is derived from the UE IPv4 (UL descriptions are rewritten as
  "from <remote> to <UE>", UL+DL of the same 5-tuple merged into
  BIDIRECTIONAL), precedence from a configurable base
- QoS decision "mcx-qos-<appSessionId>-<medCompN>": 5QI from medType (AUDIO
  65, VIDEO 67, others 69), GBR = MBR = marBwUl/Dl, ARP from resPrio
  (TS 29.514: PRIO_16 highest, configurable map, default ARP 3,
  MAY_PREEMPT, NOT_PREEMPTABLE for emergency level)
- PATCH app-sessions/{id}: RFC 7396 merge patch of the stored context
  (e.g. resPrio change / resPrio null -> ARP update)
- POST app-sessions/{id}/delete: implemented, rules removed (null in the
  notification), 204
- POST returns 201 Created with Location header (was 200 without Location
  and a problem body), proper problem details / status codes (404
  PDU_SESSION_NOT_AVAILABLE when no SM policy association is bound)
- the SM policy update notification only carries the changed/removed rules;
  AF-session rules are not persisted in the policy storage; failed
  notifications are rolled back
- session binding: the UE IP may be updated by Npcf_SMPolicyControl_Update,
  stale bindings are overwritten / ignored
- new optional "pcf.mcx_qos" configuration section (etc/config.yaml)
- docker: install libodb/libodb-mysql 2.5.0 with build2 0.18.1 since the
  build2 0.17.0 sources are no longer available (image did not build)

The raw JSON of the app session context is used for the mapping because the
generated ReservPriority / MediaType models are empty stubs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
